<p>These still work and log one console warning; they are removed in 4.0.</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <code>selection-type="checkbox"</code>: use <code>selection="multiple"</code>.
  </li>
  <li>
    <code>paginate</code> with <code>page-sizes</code>, <code>total-items</code>,
    <code>has-next</code> and <code>pagination-variant</code>: put a <code>wc-pagination</code> in
    the <code>footer</code> slot and set those attributes on it. <code>page</code> and
    <code>page-size</code> stay on the table and follow the slotted pagination.
  </li>
  <li>
    The <code>sort</code> event detail keeps <code>sortBy</code> and <code>sortOrder</code> and adds
    <code>sorts</code>; code that compares the whole detail object needs to allow the new field.
  </li>
</ul>
